      and claims that command "reports the pinned version and port plus the binary and port gates";
      measured, it prints exactly one gate row (FAIL python) on the default interpreter. CF-064 fixed
      row 3 only. Not a duplicate of CF-064.
    
    Dedupe: CF-090's premise re-measured live at this tip (ruff check exit 0; ruff format --check exit 1
    on docs/audits/cf089-census-standin.py, scripts/disk_floor.py, tests/test_disk_floor.py), so no new
    row was filed for it.
    
    Guard: gitreins guard --full failed only the tree-scoped lint arm ("3 files would be reformatted"),
    which is the pre-existing CF-090 drift measured on this same unmodified tip before any edit; the
    secrets arm was clean and the tests (full) arm passed. This board-only commit therefore uses the
    documented CF-031 core.hooksPath bypass for that invocation, disclosed here. The Tier-1 judge
    verdict for CF-091-QA is reported by the tick, not asserted here.
    
