 {"id": "CF-088", "title": "The selftest board arm accepts any valid JSON, so the gate greens a board that scripts/boardctl validate rejects", "status": "pending", "priority": "P3", "complexity": 2, "reasoning": "Measured at 400a5ab by code-factory-releng-qa-2026-11-03-15-39-07. tests/selftest.sh section 7 (\"the board is valid JSONL\") counts a line as a row when json.loads accepts it, and nothing else in the suite runs scripts/boardctl validate against the real board: section 8 exercises only --help and the missing-executable path, and grep -n validate tests/selftest.sh returns one hit that labels a lane-target test. The guard's test_command is bash tests/selftest.sh (no workflows ship), so the validator is never executed by any automated check. The row probe appends six fixtures one at a time to a clone of the tracked board and reads both verdicts: null, [], \"just-a-string\", a duplicate .id and status \"bogus_status\" each print 'PASS 69/69 rows parse / SELFTEST: PASS' while boardctl validate prints '[error] row is not a JSON object', 'duplicate task id', or 'status ... not in vocabulary' and exits 1; a row with no .status slips through both (gate PASS, validator RESULT: OK with a warning), yet such a row is invisible to the selection every foreman uses (.status==\"pending\"). The clean-board control prints 'PASS 68/68 rows parse / SELFTEST: PASS' and 'OK (21 warning(s))'. So the two checks that the repo's own Tier-2 rubric names in the same sentence (\"SELFTEST: PASS and scripts/boardctl validate prints RESULT: OK\") disagree on every non-row fixture, and the one wired into the gate is the weaker of the two. Distinct from CF-048 (a truncated final line is skipped before parsing) and CF-069 (the arm dies green when python3 emits nothing: there the arm never runs, here it runs and counts a non-row as a row).", "acceptance_criteria": "1. The selftest board arm fails on a line that is valid JSON but not a JSON object, naming the 1-based line number as boardctl validate does; the row probe's null, array and string fixtures print a gate FAIL instead of 'PASS n/n rows parse'.\n2. A duplicate .id and an out-of-vocabulary .status also fail the gate, either in the arm or by the gate running scripts/boardctl validate against the real board and propagating its exit 1; proven by the probe's duplicate-id and unknown-status arms printing a gate FAIL.\n3. A row with no .status is named as an error (not a warning) by at least one automated check, because such a row is unreachable for select(.status==\"pending\") selection; the probe's missing-status arm must stop reading 'validator: RESULT: OK'.\n4. The negative arms do not depend on boardctl being installed: when the executable is absent the arm either performs the object/duplicate/vocabulary checks itself or fails with the reason named, never a silent pass.\n5. A numbered tests/selftest.sh section covers the clean board as a positive control: it prints '<n>/<n> rows parse' with n equal to wc -l of tasks.jsonl and SELFTEST: PASS at the fixed tip, and the closing evidence shows the same section FAILing on the pre-fix tests/selftest.sh without the fix.\n6. bash tests/selftest.sh prints SELFTEST: PASS, scripts/boardctl validate prints RESULT: OK, and the closing commit is pushed with git rev-list --count origin/main..HEAD = 0.", "created_at": "2026-11-03T16:36:49Z", "updated_at": "2026-11-03T16:36:49Z", "detail": {"source": "releng-qa", "tick": "code-factory-releng-qa-2026-11-03-15-39-07", "measured_at": "400a5ab"}, "commit_hash": null, "worker_summary": null, "probe": "#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# probe: the selftest gate's board arm and the shipped validator disagree on every non-row fixture.\n# Run from the root of a code-factory checkout. Writes only inside mktemp; no network.\nset -u\nroot=$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel) || { echo \"not a git checkout\"; exit 2; }\nt=$(mktemp -d) || exit 2\ntrap 'rm -rf \"$t\"' EXIT\ngit clone -q \"$root\" \"$t/cf\" || { echo \"clone failed\"; exit 2; }\ncd \"$t/cf\" || exit 2\nB=.coding-hermes/board/tasks.jsonl\n\ngate()  { bash tests/selftest.sh 2>&1 | grep -E 'rows parse|^SELFTEST' | tr '\\n' ' '; }\nvalid() { if command -v boardctl >/dev/null 2>&1 || [ -x scripts/boardctl ]; then\n            bash scripts/boardctl validate 2>&1 | grep -E '^RESULT|^\\[error\\]' | tr '\\n' ' '\n          else echo \"validator arm SKIPPED (boardctl absent)\"; fi; }\n\narm() { # $1 label, $2 fixture text\n  git checkout -q -- \"$B\"\n  printf '%s\\n' \"$2\" >> \"$B\"\n  printf '%-26s gate: %-38s validator: %s\\n' \"$1\" \"$(gate)\" \"$(valid)\"\n  git checkout -q -- \"$B\"\n}\n\narm \"null-line\"        'null'\narm \"array-line\"       '[]'\narm \"string-line\"      '\"just-a-string\"'\narm \"duplicate-id\"     \"$(git show HEAD:$B | jq -c 'select(.id==\"CF-082\")' | head -1)\"\narm \"unknown-status\"   '{\"id\":\"CF-999\",\"title\":\"bad status\",\"priority\":\"P4\",\"status\":\"bogus_status\"}'\narm \"missing-status\"   '{\"id\":\"CF-900\",\"title\":\"no status\",\"priority\":\"P4\"}'\nprintf '%-26s gate: %-38s validator: %s\\n' \"clean-board(control)\" \"$(gate)\" \"$(valid)\"\ngit checkout -q -- \"$B\"\n"}
