 {"id":"CF-090","title":"P3 — the tree-wide lint arm is still red at origin/main on ruff-format drift, so every Tier-1 judge fails lint regardless of the graded diff","status":"complete","priority":"P3","complexity":3,"reasoning":"Measured 2026-11-03 from a pristine 'git archive' export of 03f59e8 (the parent of the CF-064 commit d26f269): 'ruff check .' -> Found 2 errors, both E702 at docs/audits/cf089-census-standin.py:32, and 'ruff format --check .' -> 3 files would be reformatted (that fixture, scripts/disk_floor.py, tests/test_disk_floor.py). Re-measured after a sibling's 02e4ae7 made the fixture E702-clean: 'ruff check .' now passes, 'ruff format --check .' still exits 1 on the same three files. The CF-064 docs commit touches none of them yet was judged stage tier1 FAIL (lint) / tier2 PASS (verdict cddf1a3d), because the lint step scans the whole tree: a clean docs diff inherits unrelated Python formatting debt and no lane can reach a green Tier-1 until it is paid down. Not CF-031 (that one is the commit hook reporting DEGRADED PASS for docs-only diffs); this is real formatter output against committed files.","acceptance_criteria":"1. On origin/main, 'ruff check .' and 'ruff format --check .' both exit 0; paste the two commands and their output into docs/audits/. 2. 'bash tests/selftest.sh' prints SELFTEST: PASS at that tip. 3. A Tier-1 judge run at the fixed tip reports lint pass (name the task id and verdict id), so the arm is demonstrably green rather than bypassed.","created_at":"2026-11-03T16:58:17Z","updated_at":"2026-11-03T17:26:41Z","detail":{"fingerprint":"a1d46e328e5bb42066121b6a03ec7c9c33ed333dac91253ae51e71469ab44932","evidence":[{"run_id":"b99b7a52","ts":"2026-11-03T17:26:41Z","tree_fp":"2c2344c3d379950a22ecab686080a6938ee26394fd1cdca2ecdc97455145a518","artifacts":["docs/audits/cf090-ruff-format.txt"]}]},"commit_hash":"3b2c81ea56b233315dc31135f6bbbc8b5ba03664","guard_result":"PASS","ci_result":"GREEN","worker_summary":"ruff check . and ruff format