ject.","acceptance_criteria":"1. The documented guard run over a fresh read-only export of the live scheduler rows prints '0 rejected' (exit 0) for every family named in docs/SCHEDULER-ADMISSION.md, or every remaining rejection is listed in a committed waiver file with a named owner and a re-check date. 2. A committed, public-safe census artifact under docs/audits/ records the totals by rejection class (no lane names, no host paths) plus the exact reproduction commands, and a later lane can diff it against a fresh run. 3. One selftest arm fails when two rows of the same family carry two different VALID repo_url roots: a primary+satellite fixture on two real git roots exits nonzero and names both lanes, while the aligned fixture exits 0. Reverting the check makes that arm fail. 4. bash tests/selftest.sh prints SELFTEST: PASS at the fixed tip.","created_at":"2026-11-03T17:25:45Z","updated_at":"2026-11-03T17:25:45Z","detail":{"fingerprint":"6242d8c178f52e9349de63fe33e0dfc2fabe90ba8df58889d77a1895c55c776a"}}
